  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ndola Diocese Integrated AIDS Programme (ZAM CAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#xb7;	To provide quality home based care and support to 25,000 people living with symptomatic HIV infection, their families and orphans in 53 community based projects in Lusaka and Central Province, 11project sites in the Copperbelt, and 8 shanty compounds in Livingstone Urban.
&#xb7;	To carry out primary, secondary and tertiary level HIV prevention work in all project sites, through community groups and schools or multifunctional centres (Ndola) or through VCT (Livingstone).
&#xb7;	To advocate and lobby at a local and national level on improved responses to the HIV and AIDS epidemic - including access to care and treatments, quality support, reducing stigma and discrimination and care of affected and vulnerable children.
&#xb7;	To enable three well established HIV and AIDS Programmes to come together to share learning and models of care and collectively increase their overall quality and impact.</narrative>
  </description>
